WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.918
Aggregate functions turn many input rows into
summary values COUNT

00:00:05.945 --> 00:00:12.118
answers how many SUM adds numeric values AVG
calculates

00:00:12.132 --> 00:00:17.079
the mean MIN finds the smallest value and MAX finds
the largest

00:00:18.831 --> 00:00:23.225
If you use an aggregate without GROUP BY PostgreSQL
normally returns one

00:00:23.252 --> 00:00:27.478
summary row for the entire input set Once you add
GROUP BY

00:00:27.662 --> 00:00:33.531
the same aggregate is calculated separately inside
each group For example

00:00:33.741 --> 00:00:39.323
AVG salary without grouping gives one company-wide
average AVG salary

00:00:39.349 --> 00:00:45.057
grouped by department gives one average for each
department Before choosing

00:00:45.083 --> 00:00:49.678
a function name the measure in plain language Are
you counting records

00:00:49.849 --> 00:00:55.599
counting known values adding revenue or averaging
completed stays That language

00:00:55.625 --> 00:00:57.678
helps you choose the correct expression
